= Dataset — Technical =

Datasets require explicit scope, schema, provenance, units, missing-value conventions, transformations, identifiers, versioning, and access conditions to be interpreted reliably. The same underlying observations can yield multiple datasets through filtering, aggregation, normalization, annotation, or derived computation.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* dataset ≠ database
* dataset ≠ raw data necessarily
* dataset ≠ verified truth

== References ==
* NIH Data Management and Sharing Policy (effective 2023), definitions and scientific-data management guidance.
* DataCite Metadata Schema, current dataset metadata practice.
* Wilkinson et al. (2016), FAIR Guiding Principles for scientific data management and stewardship.
